From: Duotek
Subject: [PATCH 0003] xlsx find: highlight only the visible matches, append the boxes at once

@silurus/ooxml 0.90.0 (dist/xlsx-27RIKj9U.js, class of the XLSX find overlay, updateOverlay()). After a search,
every match of the current sheet got an absolutely positioned <div>, appended one by one, and cellRect() reads the
layout (canvasArea.clientWidth) for each match: the browser recomputes the layout after every append, so the time
grows with the square of the match count (11,112 matches in a 100,000-row sheet: 70 s for findText, 37 s more for
findNext; 100,000 matches: the page hangs; measured on 0.89.11, the code is the same in 0.90.0). The overlay is
rebuilt on every scroll as well.
The patch skips the matches outside the visible area (no box; their cell is not drawn anyway) and appends the boxes
through one DocumentFragment. Measured after the patch on 0.89.11: 11,112 matches 1.1 s, 100,000 matches 1.0 s.
The new local names start with "dwo" so they cannot shadow a minified name of the chunk.
Apply from static/lib/silurus/ with: patch -p1 < 0003-...patch   (paths below are a/ b/ relative)

---
--- a/xlsx-27RIKj9U.js
+++ b/xlsx-27RIKj9U.js
@@ -3078,14 +3078,18 @@
